.Dd October 8, 2026
.Dt TRIX_STRERROR 3
.Os @PACKAGE_STRING@
.Sh NAME
.Nm trix_strerror
.Nd describe a status code
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In triv/expr.h
.Ft const char *
.Fn trix_strerror "int status"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn trix_strerror
function returns a static, human-readable description of a status
code.
The status codes are:
.Bl -tag -width ".Dv TRIX_ENOMEM"
.It Dv TRIX_OK
Success (0).
.It Dv TRIX_EOF
End of input.
.It Dv TRIX_ENOMEM
An allocation failed.
.It Dv TRIX_EIO
The read callback reported an error.
.It Dv TRIX_EBAD
The input is malformed.
.It Dv TRIX_ENOSYS
Not implemented yet.
.El
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn trix_strerror
function returns a string that must not be modified or freed.
An unrecognised code yields
.Qq unknown status .
